Historical diagnostic, not a current reproduction or valid repair recommendation.

An early repair experiment welded coordinates within 0.0002 mm and removed
collapsed/duplicate triangles. It reported incidence-two edges, one connected
component and coherent orientation. See historical_incomplete_weld_metrics.json.

A later version of the repair helper added vertex-manifold validation and failed:

  main()
    print(json.dumps(repair_stl(args.raw_stl, args.printable_stl), indent=2))
  repair_stl(...)
    raise ValueError("Mesh has a nonmanifold vertex")
  ValueError: Mesh has a nonmanifold vertex

This excerpt preserves the error and call names from the recorded stderr;
workstation paths and historical source line numbers have been omitted.
The experimental repair helper was subsequently replaced by STEP retessellation.
The attached validate_stl.py is the retained final read-only topology validator,
not that discarded repair implementation.
